  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Phase 1 - Rapid Response Appeal - Rohingya Refugees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">603,000 Rohingya refugees have arrived in Bangladesh since 25 August, and are living in extremely difficult conditions in the Cox&#x2019;s Bazar district. Priority needs are food, health, shelter, and WASH. The total population in need of assistance, including affected host communities, is 1.2 million.

The proposed response intends to address the immediate food needs of the newly arrived Rohingya Refugee people for 15 days. Direct food and NFIs distribution are identified as suitable strategy for responding to the immediate needs of the Rohingya Refugees.</narrative>
  </description>
